{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Program Files\\\\WindowsApps\\\\Microsoft.PowerShell_7.6.5.0_x64__8wekyb3d8bbwe\\\\pwsh.exe\" -NoProfile -Command \"Get-Content -LiteralPath 'C:\\\\Users\\\\kingd\\\\.codex\\\\plugins\\\\cache\\\\mcpserver-codex-plugin\\\\mcpserver\\\\1.106.0\\\\skills\\\\enforcement\\\\SKILL.md'; Get-Content -LiteralPath 'C:\\\\Users\\\\kingd\\\\.codex\\\\plugins\\\\cache\\\\mcpserver-codex-plugin\\\\mcpserver\\\\1.106.0\\\\skills\\\\workflow\\\\SKILL.md'; rg -n 'RomM|PowerShell.Mcp|execute_command|session logs' 'C:\\\\Users\\\\kingd\\\\.codex\\\\memories\\\\MEMORY.md'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Program Files\\\\WindowsApps\\\\Microsoft.PowerShell_7.6.5.0_x64__8wekyb3d8bbwe\\\\pwsh.exe\" -NoProfile -Command \"Get-Content -LiteralPath 'C:\\\\Users\\\\kingd\\\\.codex\\\\plugins\\\\cache\\\\mcpserver-codex-plugin\\\\mcpserver\\\\1.106.0\\\\skills\\\\enforcement\\\\SKILL.md'; Get-Content -LiteralPath 'C:\\\\Users\\\\kingd\\\\.codex\\\\plugins\\\\cache\\\\mcpserver-codex-plugin\\\\mcpserver\\\\1.106.0\\\\skills\\\\workflow\\\\SKILL.md'; rg -n 'RomM|PowerShell.Mcp|execute_command|session logs' 'C:\\\\Users\\\\kingd\\\\.codex\\\\memories\\\\MEMORY.md'\"","aggregated_output":"---\r\nname: Per-Turn Enforcement Protocol\r\ndescription: Required workflow for every user message in a Codex session. Opens a session log turn, logs all code edits, verifies builds, and closes the turn before responding. Use EVERY user message ΓÇö this is not optional.\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Overview\r\n\r\nCodex CLI lacks a hook system, so the Per-User-Message protocol from\r\n`AGENTS-README-FIRST.yaml` must be invoked manually. This skill wraps that\r\nprotocol in three scripts located in the plugin's `lib/` directory.\r\n\r\nRun `PowerShell ${CODEX_PLUGIN_ROOT}/lib/session-start.ps1 <workspace-path>` once per\r\nworkspace before Phase 1, or let `user-prompt-submit.ps1` auto-bootstrap the\r\nsession cache on first use. Runtime state is scoped under\r\n`cache/workspaces/<workspace-key>/sessions/<session-key>/`.\r\n\r\n**Every user message MUST flow through these three phases.** If you skip any\r\nphase your session log is incomplete and the workspace's AGENTS-README-FIRST\r\ncontract is violated.\r\n\r\n## Phase 1 ΓÇö Open a Turn (before any tool call)\r\n\r\nInvoke on every new user prompt **before** calling any other tool:\r\n\r\n```powershell\r\necho '{\"prompt\":\"<verbatim user message>\"}' | PowerShell ${CODEX_PLUGIN_ROOT}/lib/user-prompt-submit.ps1\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe script:\r\n- Auto-bootstraps scoped `session-state.yaml` when the marker file is trusted\r\n- Reads scoped `session-state.yaml` for the active `sessionId`\r\n- Builds a fresh `requestId` of the form `req-<yyyyMMddTHHmmssZ>-prompt-xxxx`\r\n- Calls `workflow.sessionlog.beginTurn` with the prompt as `queryText`\r\n- Writes scoped `current-turn.yaml` with `turnRequestId`, `codeEdits: 0`,\r\n  `lastBuildStatus: unknown`, `status: in_progress`\r\n- Emits a reminder via `additionalContext` that Phases 2 and 3 are mandatory\r\n\r\nIf the script outputs `status: no-session`, do not treat that as a final best-effort state. The hook has already health-checked the marker, attempts session creation when the marker timestamp changes, submits triage if creation fails after a healthy bootstrap, and records degraded recovery state under the failsafe path. Continue the user request, but preserve the `recoveryStatus`, `healthStatus`, and `failsafePath` receipt as evidence; retry session creation only after `AGENTS-README-FIRST.yaml` is rewritten or the hook reports recovery.\r\n\r\n## Phase 2 ΓÇö After Every Code Edit\r\n\r\nImmediately after you write or edit any source file\r\n(`.cs`, `.axaml`, `.xaml`, `.csproj`, `.fsproj`, `.vbproj`, `.razor`,\r\n`.cshtml`, `.ts`, `.tsx`, `.js`, `.jsx`) invoke:\r\n\r\n```powershell\r\necho '{\"tool_name\":\"Edit\",\"tool_input\":{\"file_path\":\"<absolute path>\"}}' \\\r\n  | PowerShell ${CODEX_PLUGIN_ROOT}/lib/code-verify.ps1\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe script:\r\n- Locates the nearest project file (`.csproj` / `package.json`)\r\n- Runs the matching build command (`dotnet build` or `tsc --noEmit`)\r\n- Parses the output and writes the status (`succeeded` / `failed`) to\r\n  scoped `current-turn.yaml` under `lastBuildStatus`\r\n- Records the code edit count via `workflow.sessionlog.appendActions`\r\n- Appends a `workflow.sessionlog.appendActions` entry\r\n- If the build failed, its stdout contains the first 10 errors; those\r\n  errors are the reason you must fix the build before Phase 3\r\n\r\n**Do not move on to the next edit or close the turn while\r\n`lastBuildStatus: failed` is cached.** Fix the errors first.\r\n\r\n## Phase 3 ΓÇö Close the Turn (before your final response)\r\n\r\nBefore emitting your response to the user, invoke:\r\n\r\n```powershell\r\nPowerShell ${CODEX_PLUGIN_ROOT}/lib/stop-gate.ps1\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe script checks scoped `current-turn.yaml` and returns `decision: block`\r\nwith a reason in any of these cases:\r\n- `status: in_progress` ΓÇö you forgot to call `workflow.sessionlog.completeTurn`\r\n- `codeEdits > 0 && lastBuildStatus = failed` ΓÇö build is broken\r\n\r\nWhen blocked, finish the missing step:\r\n\r\n```yaml\r\n# Complete the turn\r\ntype: request\r\npayload:\r\n  requestId: req-<new-id>\r\n  method: workflow.sessionlog.completeTurn\r\n  params:\r\n    response: |\r\n      <one-paragraph summary of what was delivered>\r\n```\r\n\r\nThen re-run `stop-gate.ps1`. Repeat until it returns `status: passed`.\r\n\r\nIf the build is intentionally left broken (rare), touch\r\nscoped `turn-accept-failure.marker` *before* the next `stop-gate.ps1` call;\r\nthe script consumes the marker on its next pass.\r\n\r\n## Contract\r\n\r\nThis protocol exists because:\r\n- `AGENTS-README-FIRST.yaml` Rule 2 requires a session log turn per user message\r\n- `AGENTS-README-FIRST.yaml` Rule 10 requires you to verify code compiles\r\n- `AGENTS-README-FIRST.yaml` \"Before Delivering Output\" requires the session\r\n  log to be current before you respond\r\n\r\nSkipping any phase leaves the contract broken. If you forget mid-turn,\r\ninvoke the missing phase as soon as you notice; partial compliance beats none.\r\n\r\n## Integration With Your Workflow\r\n\r\nThe three scripts are idempotent for the lifetime of one turn. They read\r\nand update the current session's scoped `current-turn.yaml` which is created\r\nin Phase 1 and consumed by Phase 3. The scoped cache is the source of truth\r\nfor turn state ΓÇö never infer turn status from memory or conversation.\r\n\r\n## See Also\r\n\r\n- `skills/session/SKILL.md` ΓÇö raw `workflow.sessionlog.*` commands\r\n- `skills/todo/SKILL.md` ΓÇö TODO management\r\n- `AGENTS-README-FIRST.yaml` (workspace root) ΓÇö authoritative contract\r\n---\r\nname: MCP-First Workflow\r\ndescription: This skill should be used when working in a repository that uses McpServer for session continuity, TODOs, requirements, and device validation.\r\n---\r\n## Goal\r\n\r\nMinimize repeated context reconstruction by using McpServer as the primary continuity source.\r\n\r\n## Preferred Workflow\r\n\r\n1. Read current task/session state first.\r\n2. Read recent checkpoints or deltas only if needed.\r\n3. Read TODOs or requirements only when they materially affect the current task.\r\n4. Inspect local code only when implementation work is required.\r\n5. For attached Android validation, use `adb_step` for screenshot -> inspect -> act -> screenshot loops.\r\n6. Record a checkpoint after meaningful progress, failure, or a change in plan.\r\n\r\n## Rules\r\n\r\n- Prefer the smallest MCP query that can answer the question.\r\n- Prefer deltas/checkpoints over full history.\r\n- Do not ask the user to restate recent work if session logs should already contain it.\r\n- Use MCP for continuity and mechanics.\r\n- Keep reasoning, planning, and coding decisions in Codex.\r\n\r\n## Anti-Patterns\r\n\r\nAvoid:\r\n- broad context reads before checking session state\r\n- asking the user to manually test when `adb_step` can perform the validation\r\n- reading large log histories when a recent checkpoint or delta would suffice\r\n57:scope: Required PowerShell.Mcp workflow, session-log reconciliation, Windows-service deploy, Android deploy, ngrok, and mcp-web checks.\n60:## Task 1: PowerShell.Mcp session-log reconciliation and Grok handoff, success\n64:- PowerShell.Mcp, Show-TextFiles, workflow.failsafe.drain, client.SessionLog.QueryAsync, planFile=None, todoId=None\n79:- \"Use PowerShell.Mcp. Why is that hard?\" -> in McpServer, use `mcp__powershell`, never `shell_command`; a truncated preview is not a complete read. [Task 1]\n84:- Read `AGENTS-README-FIRST.yaml`, use bounded PowerShell.Mcp reads, and send literal `planFile='None'`, `todoId='None'`; query server truth after replay/submission. Related skills: skills/mcpserver-bootstrap-todo-trust/SKILL.md and skills/mcpserver-sessionlog-agent-stdio/SKILL.md. [Task 1]\n88:- `CreateProcessAsUserW failed: 1312`, preview truncation, and generic runner error 206 do not justify bypassing the required PowerShell.Mcp route. [Task 1]\n183:- WSearch, gsudo, sc.exe, State Stopped, StartMode Disabled, PowerShell.Mcp\n246:- PowerShell.MCP 1.14.0, execute_command, AGENTS-README-FIRST.yaml, non-fast-forward, workspace-registry, Recycle Bin\n250:- `execute_command` replaced `invoke_expression`; validate schemas/templates and `git diff --check`. Registry API is authoritative for workspace deletion; non-fast-forward is a hard stop. [Task 1]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
