{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"powershell","tool":"execute_command","arguments":{"pipeline":"Show-TextFiles 'AGENTS-README-FIRST.yaml' -LineRange 252,294\nShow-TextFiles 'docs/plans/PLAN-PHASE12-CLOSEOUT.md' -LineRange 1,52\nShow-TextFiles 'C:\\Users\\kingd\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\PowerShell.MCP.Output\\pwsh_output_20260915_175717_296_hi4ggw0x.uti.txt' -Pattern 'signature|nonce|sessionId|currentTurn|trusted|requestId|pluginRoot'","timeout_seconds":30},"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Γ£ô Pipeline executed successfully | Window: #29172 Virgo | Status: Ready | Pipeline: Show-TextFiles 'AGENTS-READ... | Duration: 0.47s | Location [FileSystem]: F:\\GitHub\\RomM\r\n\n\u001b[1m==> AGENTS-README-FIRST.yaml <==\u001b[0m\r\n252:   ## PowerShell.MCP Command Routing\r\n253:   For every PowerShell Core (`pwsh`) invocation on every operating system:\r\n254:   - Use PowerShell.MCP 1.14.0 or newer from PSGallery as the command runner. Install or update it with `Install-PSResource PowerShell.MCP` when the agent environment does not provide a current version.\r\n255:   - `execute_command` is the primary MCP tool for PowerShell cmdlets, CLI tools, navigation, builds, tests, file-system work, and process management. Do not use the removed `invoke_expression` name. Host-qualified names depend on the configured server key: for example, `mcp__powershell__execute_command` for `powershell` and `mcp__pwsh__execute_command` for `pwsh`.\r\n256:   - Calling `start_console` first is optional because `execute_command` auto-starts or reuses a console. Call `start_console` explicitly only to pre-warm at `start_location`, show a banner, allocate a sub-agent console, or force an additional console by supplying `reason`; omit `reason` when reuse is preferred.\r\n257:   - Use `get_current_location` when the current PowerShell context matters. For a sub-agent, call `start_console` with `is_subagent=true`, retain the returned `agent_id`, and pass it on every later PowerShell.MCP tool call.\r\n258:   - When a command continues after the call returns, use `wait_for_completion` to retrieve the cached result instead of running `Start-Sleep`. Use `cancel` for an interruptible pipeline or native CLI, and `close_console` for a non-interruptible command or PowerShell host prompt. If `close_console` reports that a human is typing, only repeat the same PID call when confirming that the console should be closed.\r\n259:   - In 1.14.0, blocking timeouts are end-to-end deadlines and are capped at 170 seconds for Claude Code and 50 seconds for other or unidentified clients unless a lower limit applies. A timed-out command keeps running and its result is cached for a later tool call.\r\n260:   - Route `pwsh` commands through a PowerShell.MCP session instead of launching ad hoc PowerShell processes. On Windows, reuse one session for the workspace and route `node` invocations through it as well.\r\n261:   - When PowerShell.MCP must launch PowerShell Core directly, invoke `pwsh.exe` with `-NoProfile -NonInteractive`. Do not use `powershell.exe`.\r\n262:   - The PowerShell escape character is the backtick `` ` ``, not the backslash. Never use C or bash-style `\\\"` escaping inside PowerShell command strings.\r\n263:   - Prefer single-quoted PowerShell strings for literal regex, paths, JSON/YAML snippets, and text containing pipeline characters such as `|`.\r\n264:   - When a command needs nested quoting, choose one of these patterns before improvising: `-File` with explicit arguments; piping stdin to the called tool or script; single-quoted or double-quoted here-strings; `-EncodedCommand` for complex inline PowerShell; or correct backtick escaping for embedded PowerShell quotes.\r\n265:   - If a regex or literal argument contains `|`, `&`, `;`, parentheses, braces, or quotes, verify it is inside a single PowerShell argument before running.\r\n266:   - For text reads and edits inside PowerShell.MCP, use `Show-TextFiles`, `Add-LinesToFile`, `Update-LinesInFile`, `Update-MatchInFile`, and `Remove-LinesFromFile`; pass literal content through `var1` to `var4`. Version 1.12.0 and newer stage replacements beside the target, so do not apply the obsolete same-volume `TEMP`/`TMP` workaround. Re-read or diff every edit before claiming it landed.\r\n267:   ## Byrd Development Process\r\n268:   `Byrd Dev Process`, `BDP`, `BPDv4`, and `Byrd Development Process` refer to `F:\\GitHub\\McpServer\\docs\\Development-Process-draft-v4.md`.\r\n269: \r\n270:   ## Federation Topology\r\n271:   - To identify hub/proxy topology, call the supported federation status surface, preferably through your required plugin or client wrapper: `/mcpserver/federation/status`. - Status fields to report when relevant: `role`, `configuredRole`, `hubBaseUrl`, `proxyId`, `proxyCount`, `hostedWorkspaceCount`, `queueDepth`, `fanoutDepth`, `conflictCount`, and `staleReadStatus`. - `Standalone` serves local workspaces only. `DirectProxy` is the existing point-to-point proxy mode. `Hub` is authoritative for enrolled proxies and global workspace inventory. `LocalProxy` forwards MCP requests to `hubBaseUrl` and queues mutating requests during hub outages. - LocalProxy queued writes return `202 Accepted` with `X-Mcp-Queued: true` and `X-Mcp-Operation-Id`. Treat the write as optimistic until the hub acknowledges it. - If `queueDepth`, `fanoutDepth`, `conflictCount`, or stale-read status is non-zero/non-clear, include that in session log status and avoid claiming federation synchronization is complete.\r\n272: \r\n273:   ## Per User Message\r\n274:   1. Post a new session log turn before starting work.\r\n275:   2. Complete the user's request.\r\n276:   3. Update the turn with results and actions when done.\r\n277: \r\n278:   ## Re-run Full Session Start Only If\r\n279:   - The user explicitly says \"Start Session\". - Signature verification fails. - /health fails. - /health nonce verification fails. - Any /mcpserver/* call returns 401. - The marker endpoint/key changes after a server restart.\r\n280: \r\n281:   ## Continuing After a Server Restart\r\n282:   The workspace API key rotates on every server restart, so an in-flight agent will begin seeing 401 on /mcpserver/* calls. When that happens, resume through your required agent plugin - do not hand-roll raw REST for session, TODO, or requirements work:\r\n283:   1. Treat the first 401 (or a /health failure) as a restart signal and stop using the cached API key immediately.\r\n284:   2. Re-read this marker file (AGENTS-README-FIRST.yaml) for the rotated apiKey and current endpoints.\r\n285:   3. Re-verify trust before resuming: recompute the marker signature with the new key and call /health with a fresh nonce.\r\n286:   4. Re-bootstrap and resume through your required agent plugin. Codex: run `Invoke-CodexMcpPlugin.ps1 -Command Status` to re-establish marker trust, health nonce, workspace, and the current session/turn, then continue with `Invoke-CodexMcpPlugin.ps1 -Command Invoke -Method <method> -Params <yaml>`. Other agents: re-run the plugin session-start hook/command, then continue via the plugin session tools.\r\n287:   5. Recover the open turn instead of starting over: query session history through the plugin (workflow.sessionlog.queryHistory), find the in-progress turn, then keep updating and complete it via the plugin. Do not open a duplicate session for the same work.\r\n288:   5a. Treat `deprecated: true` on successful `workflow.*` results as metadata, not wrapper failure. Treat an empty `workflow.sessionlog.queryHistory` result as a valid no-match result. Re-check the workspace current directory, explicit `agent` or `sourceType`, and plugin cache/session state through the wrapper; do not use raw REST merely because history is empty or marked deprecated.\r\n289:   6. If the plugin cannot re-establish trust after the restart, record `MCP_PLUGIN_UNAVAILABLE:<Agent>` and continue with non-MCP local diagnosis only.\r\n290: \r\n291:   ## Rules\r\n292:   0. NEVER write to TODO.yaml directly.\r\n293:   1. Generate SessionId values using `session.init` (REPL) or `New-McpSessionLogSlug -Agent <SourceType> -Model <Model>` (PowerShell module), then create session logs with `session.new` (REPL) or `New-McpSessionLog -SessionId` (PowerShell). Do not handcraft SessionId values.\r\n294:   1a. Agents must identify themselves accurately in session logs. `sourceType` and the SessionId `<Agent>` prefix must use the agent's real identity in Pascal-Case. Do not use lowercase forms, placeholders, or legacy aliases.\r\n\u001b[1m==> docs\\plans\\PLAN-PHASE12-CLOSEOUT.md <==\u001b[0m\r\n  1: # Plan: close PLAN-ROMMCLIENT-001 phases 1 and 2\r\n  2: \r\n  3: **Date:** 2026-09-15\r\n  4: **Source:** Codex `gpt-6-astra` review + HV (`docs/receipts/codex-phase12-20260915.request-response.jsonl`)\r\n  5: **Verdict:** DISAGREE. Do not mark Iteration 1 or 2 complete.\r\n  6: \r\n  7: Phases:\r\n  8: - Phase 1 / Iteration 1: RomM auth handlers (FR-AUTH-001/002, IMPL-ROMMCLIENT-001)\r\n  9: - Phase 2 / Iteration 2: system, platforms, ROM read, pagination\r\n 10: \r\n 11: Tests Codex re-ran: `dotnet test tests/RomM.Client.Tests/RomM.Client.Tests.csproj -c Release` = 46 passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped. Green suite is **not** DoD.\r\n 12: \r\n 13: ## Blocking remediations (Byrd order)\r\n 14: \r\n 15: ### R1. Replace placeholder client FRs with testable AC\r\n 16: \r\n 17: **FAIL:** wiki/MCP exports still have \"Placeholder requirement backfilled\" for FR-AUTH-001, FR-AUTH-002, FR-SYS-001, FR-PLT-001, FR-ROM-001..004, FR-TASK-001/002. Mappings omit those IDs. No TEST-AUTH record.\r\n 18: \r\n 19: **Work:**\r\n 20: 1. Update each FR in MCP (`workspacePath` `F:\\GitHub\\RomM`) with real body + numbered AC (Bearer `rmm_`, Basic, OAuth refresh skew, 401/403 types, heartbeat schema, platforms list/get, roms page fields, pagination).\r\n 21: 2. Create TEST-AUTH, TEST-SYS, TEST-PLT, TEST-ROM covering those AC by test class/method.\r\n 22: 3. Cre